# 1640s (2026-10-18): Gustavus Adolphus's salvee - march in close, one great volley, then in.
drill "Salvee"
era 1640s
about "Gustavus's way: march in close, give one great salvo at twenty-five metres, then go in with sword and butt while they reel."
type Musketeer
dials aggression 0.80 discipline 0.85 cohesion 0.85 cover 0.00 patience 0.90 nerve 0.70

sergeant:
  when horse charging and enemy within 35       -> hold; form tight; stand fast; volley
  when phase is fired and enemy within 30       -> charge
  when enemy within 28                          -> hold; form tight; volley; set phase fired
  otherwise                                     -> advance; form tight; hold fire

man:
  when volley called and loaded                 -> fire
  otherwise                                     -> follow sergeant
